.TH DEFW-PYTHON 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
defw-python \- run a Python application through the QFw DEFw executor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B defw-python
.I script
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B defw-python
locates the DEFw executor under
.BR DEFW_PREFIX ,
verifies that its embedded Python major and minor version match the active
Python environment, exposes that environment's site packages, and invokes the
script through DEFw.
.PP
Normal applications use this entry point indirectly through
.BR qfw-srun (1).
It is also useful for low-level diagnostics that require a DEFw agent context.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIRTUAL_ENV
Selects the application Python environment when it contains
.IR bin/python .
.TP
.B DEFW_PREFIX
Selects the DEFw installation. The activated QFw environment supplies the
default.
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Is extended with active-environment site-package directories.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The DEFw wrapper or application status is returned. Missing executors and
Python-version mismatches return nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-activate (1),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw (7)
